[LINK: (H:YFA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=H:YFA&redirect=no]  [LINK: (H:YFA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H:YFA]

The topic of the article must be  [LINK: (notable) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:N] : it must have  [LINK: (in-depth coverage) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:SIGCOV]  in  [LINK: (reliable sources) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:RS]  that are  [LINK: (independent) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Independent_sources]  of the topic.

If you are  [LINK: (connected to the topic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:COI] , don't write about it. Find another topic instead.

Make sure there  [LINK: (isn't already an article) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Your_first_article#Search_for_an_existing_article]  about the topic.

The article you write must include  [LINK: (citations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:INLINECITE]  to the sources you used.

Use your own words to write the article; you must not  [LINK: (copy from sources) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:COPYRIGHT]  word-for-word.

Don't use  [LINK: (large language models) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:LLM]  (LLMs).

Creating an article is one of the more difficult tasks on Wikipedia, and you'll have a higher chance of success if you  [LINK: (help out with other tasks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Homepage]  first to learn more about how Wikipedia works. You can always come back to create an article later; there is  [LINK: (no rush) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:There_is_no_deadline] !

